+// Call sites (D-157-39, build 28 item 2; audit C12): a web call needs its scripts and, on most services, the desktop
+// page, so the phone identity and Very slow link's no-JavaScript rule broke calls in the very mode a satellite user
+// switches on. A site is a call site when the user allowed it the camera or the microphone (remembered, or for this
+// tab only), or when it is on the local list below (a site without scripts can never ask for the microphone). It
+// gets its desktop identity and its scripts at every level. The list is local data: nothing is fetched.
+const CALL_SITES_PREF = "gorilla.linkmode.call_sites";
+const CALL_PERMISSIONS = ["camera", "microphone"];
 
